    ],
    "text": "[A1][/A1]NAME",
    "placeholders": {
     "A1": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_195_01\" id=\"tag_17_195_01\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "blockquote_00002",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     13
    ],
    "text": "ftruncate — truncate a file to a specified length",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00003",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     15
    ],
    "text": "[A2][/A2]SYNOPSIS",
    "placeholders": {
     "A2": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_195_02\" id=\"tag_17_195_02\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00004",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     17,
     1
    ],
    "text": "[CODE3]",
    "placeholders": {
     "CODE3": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<code><tt>#include &lt;<a href=\"../basedefs/unistd.h.html\">unistd.h</a>&gt;<br>\n<br>\nint ftruncate(int</tt> <i>fildes</i><tt>, off_t</tt> <i>length</i><tt>);<br></tt></code>"
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00005",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     19
    ],
    "text": "[A4][/A4]DESCRIPTION",
    "placeholders": {
     "A4": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_195_03\" id=\"tag_17_195_03\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00006",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     1
    ],
    "text": "If [I5]fildes[/I5] is not a valid file descriptor open for writing, the [I6]ftruncate[/I6]() function shall fail.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I5": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I6": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00007",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     3
    ],
    "text": "If [I7]fildes[/I7] refers to a regular file, the [I8]ftruncate[/I8]() function shall cause the size of the file to be truncated to\n[I9]length[/I9]. If the size of the file previously exceeded [I10]length[/I10], the extra data shall no longer be available to reads on\nthe file. If the file previously was smaller than this size, [I11]ftruncate[/I11]() shall increase the size of the file. If the file\nsize is increased, the extended area shall appear as if it were zero-filled. The value of the seek pointer shall not be modified by\na call to [I12]ftruncate[/I12]().",
    "placeholders": {
     "I7": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I8": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I9": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I10": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I11": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I12": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00008",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     5
    ],
    "text": "Upon successful completion, if [I13]fildes[/I13] refers to a regular file, [I14]ftruncate[/I14]() shall mark for update the last data\nmodification and last file status change timestamps of the file and the S_ISUID and S_ISGID bits of the file mode may be cleared.\nIf the [I15]ftruncate[/I15]() function is unsuccessful, the file is unaffected.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I13": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I14": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I15": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00009",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     7
    ],
    "text": "If the request would cause the file size to exceed the soft file size limit for the process, the request shall fail\n[S16][[A17]XSI[/A17]][/S16] [IMG18]\n&nbsp;and the implementation shall generate a SIGXFSZ signal for the thread. [IMG19]",
    "placeholders": {
     "S16": {
      "open": "<sup>",
      "close": "</sup>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A17": {
      "open": "<a href=\"javascript:open_code(&#x27;XSI&#x27;)\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "IMG18": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<img src=\"../images/opt-start.gif\" alt=\"[Option Start]\" border=\"0\">"
     },
     "IMG19": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<img src=\"../images/opt-end.gif\" alt=\"[Option End]\" border=\"0\">"
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00010",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     9
    ],
    "text": "If [I20]fildes[/I20] is a file descriptor open for writing and refers to a file that is neither a regular file nor a shared memory\nobject, the result is unspecified.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I20": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00011",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     11
    ],
    "text": "[S21][[A22]SHM[/A22]][/S21] [IMG23]\nIf [I24]fildes[/I24] refers to a shared memory object, [I25]ftruncate[/I25]() shall set the size of the shared memory object to\n[I26]length[/I26]. [IMG27]",
    "placeholders": {
     "S21": {
      "open": "<sup>",
      "close": "</sup>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A22": {
      "open": "<a href=\"javascript:open_code(&#x27;SHM&#x27;)\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "IMG23": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<img src=\"../images/opt-start.gif\" alt=\"[Option Start]\" border=\"0\">"
     },
     "I24": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I25": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I26": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "IMG27": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<img src=\"../images/opt-end.gif\" alt=\"[Option End]\" border=\"0\">"
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00012",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     13
    ],
    "text": "If the effect of [I28]ftruncate[/I28]() is to decrease the size of a memory mapped file [S29][[A30]SHM[/A30]][/S29] [IMG31] &nbsp;or a shared\nmemory object [IMG32] &nbsp;and whole pages beyond the new end were\npreviously mapped, then the whole pages beyond the new end shall be discarded.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I28": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "S29": {
      "open": "<sup>",
      "close": "</sup>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A30": {
      "open": "<a href=\"javascript:open_code(&#x27;SHM&#x27;)\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "IMG31": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<img src=\"../images/opt-start.gif\" alt=\"[Option Start]\" border=\"0\">"
     },
     "IMG32": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<img src=\"../images/opt-end.gif\" alt=\"[Option End]\" border=\"0\">"
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00013",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     15
    ],
    "text": "References to discarded pages shall result in the generation of a SIGBUS signal.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00014",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     17
    ],
    "text": "If the effect of [I33]ftruncate[/I33]() is to increase the size of a memory object, it is unspecified whether the contents of any\nmapped pages between the old end-of-file and the new are flushed to the underlying object.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I33": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00015",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     23
    ],
    "text": "[A34][/A34]RETURN VALUE",
    "placeholders": {
     "A34": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_195_04\" id=\"tag_17_195_04\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00016",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     25,
     1
    ],
    "text": "Upon successful completion, [I35]ftruncate[/I35]() shall return 0; otherwise, -1 shall be returned and [I36]errno[/I36] set to indicate\nthe error.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I35": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I36": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00017",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     27
    ],
    "text": "[A37][/A37]ERRORS",
    "placeholders": {
     "A37": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_195_05\" id=\"tag_17_195_05\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00018",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [I38]ftruncate[/I38]() function shall fail if:",
    "placeholders": {
     "I38": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00019",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     3,
     3
    ],
    "text": "[EBADF] or [EINVAL]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00020",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     3,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The [I39]fildes[/I39] argument is not a file descriptor open for writing.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I39": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00021",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     3,
     7
    ],
    "text": "[EFBIG] or [EINVAL]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00022",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     3,
     9
    ],
    "text": "The [I40]length[/I40] argument is greater than the maximum file size.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I40": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00023",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     3,
     11
    ],
    "text": "[EFBIG]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00024",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     3,
     13
    ],
    "text": "The [I41]length[/I41] argument exceeds the file size limit of the process. [S42][[A43]XSI[/A43]][/S42] [IMG44] &nbsp;A SIGXFSZ\nsignal shall also be generated for the thread. [IMG45]",
    "placeholders": {
     "I41": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "S42": {
      "open": "<sup>",
      "close": "</sup>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A43": {
      "open": "<a href=\"javascript:open_code(&#x27;XSI&#x27;)\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "IMG44": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<img src=\"../images/opt-start.gif\" alt=\"[Option Start]\" border=\"0\">"
     },
     "IMG45": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<img src=\"../images/opt-end.gif\" alt=\"[Option End]\" border=\"0\">"
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00025",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     3,
     15
    ],
    "text": "[EFBIG]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00026",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     3,
     17
    ],
    "text": "The file is a regular file and [I46]length[/I46] is greater than the offset maximum established in the open file description\nassociated with [I47]fildes[/I47].",
    "placeholders": {
     "I46": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I47": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00027",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     3,
     19
    ],
    "text": "[EINTR]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
