    "text": "First released in Issue 4, Version 2.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00046",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     59
    ],
    "text": "[A62][/A62]Issue 5",
    "placeholders": {
     "A62": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_195_12\" id=\"tag_17_195_12\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00047",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     61,
     1
    ],
    "text": "Moved from X/OPEN UNIX extension to BASE and aligned with [I63]ftruncate[/I63]() in the POSIX Realtime Extension. Specifically, the\nDESCRIPTION is extensively reworded and [EROFS] is added to the list of mandatory errors that can be returned by\n[I64]ftruncate[/I64]().",
    "placeholders": {
     "I63": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I64": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00048",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     61,
     3
    ],
    "text": "Large File Summit extensions are added.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00049",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     63
    ],
    "text": "[A65][/A65]Issue 6",
    "placeholders": {
     "A65": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_195_13\" id=\"tag_17_195_13\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00050",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     65,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [A66][I67]truncate[/I67]()[/A66] function is split out into a separate reference page.",
    "placeholders": {
     "A66": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/truncate.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I67": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00051",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     65,
     3
    ],
    "text": "The following new requirements on POSIX implementations derive from alignment with the Single UNIX Specification:",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00052",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     65,
     5,
     1,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The DESCRIPTION is changed to indicate that if the file size is changed, and if the file is a regular file, the S_ISUID and\nS_ISGID bits in the file mode may be cleared.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00053",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     65,
     7
    ],
    "text": "The following changes were made to align with the IEEE&nbsp;P1003.1a draft standard:",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00054",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     65,
     9,
     1,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The DESCRIPTION text is updated.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00055",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     65,
     11
    ],
    "text": "XSI-conformant systems are required to increase the size of the file if the file was previously smaller than the size\nrequested.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00056",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     67
    ],
    "text": "[A68][/A68]Issue 7",
    "placeholders": {
     "A68": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_195_14\" id=\"tag_17_195_14\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00057",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     69,
     1
    ],
    "text": "Austin Group Interpretation 1003.1-2001 #056 is applied, revising the ERRORS section (although the [EINVAL] &quot;may fail&quot; error\nwas subsequently removed during review of the XSI option).",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00058",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     69,
     3
    ],
    "text": "Functionality relating to the Memory Protection and Memory Mapped Files options is moved to the Base.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00059",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     69,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The DESCRIPTION is updated so that a call to [I69]ftruncate[/I69]() when the file is smaller than the size requested will increase\nthe size of the file. Previously, non-XSI-conforming implementations were allowed to increase the size of the file or fail.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I69": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00060",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     69,
     7
    ],
    "text": "Changes are made related to support for finegrained timestamps.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00061",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     71
    ],
    "text": "[A70][/A70]Issue 8",
    "placeholders": {
     "A70": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_195_15\" id=\"tag_17_195_15\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00062",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     73,
     1
    ],
    "text": "Austin Group Defect 308 is applied, clarifying the handling of [EFBIG] errors.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00063",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     73,
     3
    ],
    "text": "Austin Group Defect 1169 is applied, removing a redundant statement that [I71]ftruncate[/I71]() fails if [I72]fildes[/I72] refers to a\ndirectory.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I71": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I72": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00064",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     73,
     5
    ],
    "text": "Austin Group Defect 1381 is applied, adding a second condition to the [EINVAL] error and rearranging the ERRORS section into\nalphabetical order.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00065",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     73,
     7
    ],
    "text": "Austin Group Defect 1669 is applied, removing XSI shading from part of the [EFBIG] error relating to the file size limit for the\nprocess.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00066",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     79
    ],
    "text": "&nbsp;",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   }
  ]
 }
}